course: dictionary
lesson: 2912
title: Dozen and dozens
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dozen means twelve. A dozen eggs is 12 eggs, and a dozen rolls is 12 rolls. Shops often sell eggs, rolls and cookies by the dozen.
explain: «Dozens» has an s on the end and means a lot, many. «Dozens of people» means many people, not exactly twelve. To check, swap in the word many: «work that once took many people» still makes sense.
explain: Some phrases use the same idea. Half a dozen is 6, and a baker's dozen is 13. For «dozens», the clues are the words around it. «Job hunting means ... often dozens before getting anywhere» tells you many applications, and many get no reply.
fact: A dozen means 12.
fact: Half a dozen means 6.
fact: A baker's dozen means 13.
fact: «Dozens of» means many.
fact: N dozen means N × 12, so 3 dozen is 36.
exercise: How many eggs are in a dozen eggs? | 13 | 10 | *12 | 6
exercise: «A combine harvester ... doing work that once took dozens of people with sickles.» What does dozens mean here? | One | Exactly twelve | Two | *Many
exercise: What is half a dozen? | 3 | 12 | 4 | *6
test: A baker's dozen is how many? | 11 | 14 | 12 | *13
test: «Within one lifetime those patches broke into many small ones ... dozens of separate pictures.» What does dozens mean here? | *Many | Exactly twelve | Two | Just one
exam: Jayden buys 3 dozen cookies. How many cookies does he buy? | *36 | 15 | 30 | 24
